cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use leanstats, please cite it as below."
title: leanstats
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 and mathlib proofs that Holm's step-down procedure controls the family-wise error
  rate under arbitrary dependence, that Clopper-Pearson intervals have coverage at least
  1 - alpha for every success probability, and of Ville's inequality for non-negative
  supermartingales.
type: software
authors:
  - name: h-a-forster
repository-code: "https://github.com/h-a-forster/leanstats"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-30"
keywords:
  - lean4
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - multiple testing
  - confidence intervals
  - martingales
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Holm
        given-names: Sture
    title: "A simple sequentially rejective multiple test procedure"
    journal: "Scandinavian Journal of Statistics"
    volume: 6
    year: 1979
    start: 65
    end: 70
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Clopper
        given-names: C. J.
      - family-names: Pearson
        given-names: E. S.
    title: "The use of confidence or fiducial limits illustrated in the case of the binomial"
    journal: Biometrika
    volume: 26
    year: 1934
    start: 404
    end: 413
    doi: 10.1093/biomet/26.4.404
  - type: book
